# ROS 2 Package Structure Standards —

## 🎯 Core Principles

### Mandatory Structure

Every ROS 2 package MUST follow this organization:

```
package_name/
├── CMakeLists.txt              # Build configuration
├── package.xml                 # Package metadata
├── README.md                   # Package overview
├── include/package_name/       # Public headers
│   ├── core/                   # Business logic (OR logic/)
│   │   ├── *.hpp              # Domain entities, controllers
│   │   └── *_config.hpp       # Configuration structures
│   └── ros2_interface/         # ROS2 layer (OR ros2/)
│       ├── *_node.hpp         # ROS2 node classes
│       └── *_adapter.hpp      # Message conversion
├── src/
│   ├── core/                   # Business logic implementation
│   │   └── *.cpp
│   ├── ros2_interface/         # ROS2 implementation
│   │   └── *.cpp
│   └── main.cpp               # Entry point only
├── launch/                     # Launch files (.launch.py)
│   ├── *_control.launch.py    # Individual node launch
│   └── *_system.launch.py     # Complete system launch
├── config/                     # Configuration files
│   └── *.yaml                 # Parameter files
├── test/                       # Tests
│   ├── test_*.cpp             # Unit tests (gtest)
│   └── test_*_e2e.py          # E2E tests (launch_testing)
└── docs/                       # Documentation
    ├── README.md
    ├── architecture/
    ├── diagrams/
    ├── interfaces/
    └── testing/
```

## 🏗️ Directory Organization

### Business Logic Layer (core/ or logic/)

**Purpose:** Pure C++ business logic, NO ROS2 dependencies

**Contents:**

- Domain entities and value objects
- Business controllers and algorithms
- Configuration structures
- Pure C++ interfaces

**Rules:**

- NEVER include rclcpp headers
- NEVER use ROS2 message types
- Use only standard C++ types (std::string, std::vector, std::chrono, etc.)
- All business rules testable without ROS2

**Example Files:**

- `pump_controller.hpp/cpp` - Pump control logic
- `flow_corrector.hpp/cpp` - Flow correction algorithm
- `motor.hpp/cpp` - Motor control logic
- `turret.hpp/cpp` - Turret coordination logic
- `*_config.hpp/cpp` - Configuration structures

### Architecture Patterns

**Pattern 1: Modular Architecture (Recommended)**

```
package_name/
├── src/core/              # Business logic (ROS-independent)
├── src/ros2/    # ROS2 interface layer
├── include/package_name/
│   ├── core/              # Core headers
│   └── ros2/    # ROS2 headers
└── CMakeLists.txt         # Separate libraries
```


### ROS2 Interface Layer (ros2_interface/ or ros2/)

**Purpose:** ROS2 integration only, delegates to business logic

**Contents:**

- ROS2 node classes
- Message/service adapters
- Topic publishers/subscribers
- Service servers/clients
- Parameter loading

**Rules:**

- ALL ROS2 dependencies confined here
- Minimal business logic - delegate to core/
- Handle ROS2 message conversion
- Manage ROS2 lifecycle

**Example Files:**

- `pump_node.hpp/cpp` - ROS2 node for pump
- `motor_node.hpp/cpp` - ROS2 node for motor
- `turret_node.hpp/cpp` - ROS2 node for turret
- `ros2_adapter.hpp/cpp` - Message conversion

### Main Entry Point

**src/main.cpp:**

```cpp
#include "package_name/ros2_interface/node_name.hpp"

int main(int argc, char** argv) {
    rclcpp::init(argc, argv);
    auto node = std::make_shared<package_name::ros2_interface::NodeName>();
    rclcpp::spin(node);
    rclcpp::shutdown();
    return 0;
}
```

**Rules:**

- ONLY initialization and spinning
- NO business logic
- NO parameter loading
- Keep under 15 lines

### Launch Files

**Naming:**

- `package_control.launch.py` - Single node launch
- `package_system.launch.py` - Multi-node system launch

**Structure:**

```python
from launch import LaunchDescription
from launch_ros.actions import Node

def generate_launch_description():
    return LaunchDescription([
        Node(
            package='package_name',
            executable='node_name',
            name='node_name',
            parameters=[config_file],
            output='screen'
        )
    ])
```

**Rules:**

- Use Node actions, not ExecuteProcess for ROS2 nodes
- Load parameters from config/ directory
- Set output='screen' for visibility
- Document all launch arguments

### Configuration Files

**Location:** `config/*.yaml`

**Structure:**

```yaml
/**:
  ros__parameters:
    # Hardware parameters
    device_id: "device_001"

    # Motion parameters
    max_speed: 100.0
    min_limit: -180.0
    max_limit: 180.0

    # ROS2 interface
    status_rate_hz: 10.0
```

**Rules:**

- Use `/**:` for node-agnostic parameters
- Group related parameters
- Include units in parameter names or comments
- Provide sensible defaults in code

### Tests

**Pattern 1: Modular Architecture Testing**

**Unit Tests (test\_\*.cpp):**

- Test business logic only (core/ classes)
- Use Google Test framework
- NO ROS2 initialization
- Fast execution (< 1s per test)
- Link against core library only

**E2E Tests (test\_\*\_e2e.py):**

- Test complete ROS2 system
- Use launch_testing framework
- Test services, topics, parameters
- Verify end-to-end behavior

**Pattern 2: Simplified Architecture Testing**

**E2E Tests (test\_\*\_e2e.py):**

- Test complete ROS2 system
- Use launch_testing framework
- Test services, topics, parameters
- Verify end-to-end behavior
- Primary testing method for simplified packages

### Documentation

**Mandatory Files:**

- `README.md` - Package overview
- `docs/architecture/architecture.md` - System design
- `docs/diagrams/system-architecture.md` - Mermaid diagrams
- `docs/interfaces/messages.md` - ROS2 interfaces
- `docs/testing/README.md` - Testing strategy

## 📦 Package Types

### Control Packages

**Example:** pump_control, motor_control, turret_control

**Structure:**

- `include/{package}/core/` - Control algorithms
- `include/{package}/ros2_interface/` - ROS2 nodes
- Tests for both layers

### Interface Packages

**Example:** pump_control_interfaces, turret_interfaces

**Structure:**

```
package_interfaces/
├── msg/           # Message definitions
├── srv/           # Service definitions
├── action/        # Action definitions
├── CMakeLists.txt
├── package.xml
└── README.md
```

**Rules:**

- Separate package for interfaces
- Clear, documented message fields
- Follow ROS2 naming conventions

### Library Packages

**Example:** robot_common

**Structure:**

- Reusable components
- No ROS2 node executables
- Exported libraries for other packages

## 🔧 Build Configuration

### CMakeLists.txt

**Pattern 1: Modular Architecture (Recommended)**

```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.18)
project(package_name LANGUAGES CXX)

# Flags
if(CMAKE_COMPILER_IS_GNUCXX OR CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "Clang")
  add_compile_options(-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wunused-parameter -Werror)
endif()

# C++20 standard
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD            20 )
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED   ON )
set(CMAKE_CXX_EXTENSIONS          OFF)
set(CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS ON )

# Find dependencies
find_package(ament_cmake REQUIRED)
find_package(rclcpp REQUIRED)
find_package(package_interfaces REQUIRED)

set(DEPENDENCIES
  rclcpp
  package_interfaces
)

# Include directories
include_directories(include)

# Core library (business logic - NO ROS2 dependencies)
add_library(${PROJECT_NAME}_core SHARED
    src/core/controller.cpp
    src/core/config.cpp
    # ... other core sources
)

# ROS2 library
add_library(${PROJECT_NAME}_ros2 SHARED
    src/ros2_interface/controller_node.cpp
    # ... other ros2 sources
)
target_link_libraries(${PROJECT_NAME}_ros2
  ${PROJECT_NAME}_core
)
ament_target_dependencies(${PROJECT_NAME}_ros2 ${DEPENDENCIES})
ament_export_targets(export_${PROJECT_NAME} HAS_LIBRARY_TARGET)
ament_export_dependencies(${DEPENDENCIES})

# ROS2 node executable
add_executable(${PROJECT_NAME}_node
    src/main.cpp
)
target_link_libraries(${PROJECT_NAME}_node ${PROJECT_NAME}_ros2)
ament_target_dependencies(${PROJECT_NAME}_node ${DEPENDENCIES})

# Install
install(
  TARGETS ${PROJECT_NAME}_core ${PROJECT_NAME}_ros2
  EXPORT export_${PROJECT_NAME}
  ARCHIVE DESTINATION lib
  LIBRARY DESTINATION lib
  RUNTIME DESTINATION bin
  INCLUDES DESTINATION include
)
install(
  TARGETS ${PROJECT_NAME}_node
  DESTINATION lib/${PROJECT_NAME}
)
install(DIRECTORY include/ DESTINATION include)
install(DIRECTORY launch/ config/ DESTINATION share/${PROJECT_NAME})

# Testing
if(BUILD_TESTING)
    find_package(ament_cmake_gtest REQUIRED)
    ament_add_gtest(${PROJECT_NAME}_core_test
        tests/test_core.cpp
    )
    target_link_libraries(${PROJECT_NAME}_core_test ${PROJECT_NAME}_core)
    ament_add_gtest(${PROJECT_NAME}_ros2_test
        tests/test_ros2.cpp
    )
    target_link_libraries(${PROJECT_NAME}_ros2_test ${PROJECT_NAME}_ros2)
endif()

# Packaging
ament_package()
```

**Pattern 2: Simplified Architecture (Alternative)**

```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.18)
project(package_name LANGUAGES CXX)

# Flags
if(CMAKE_COMPILER_IS_GNUCXX OR CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "Clang")
  add_compile_options(-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wunused-parameter -Werror)
endif()

# C++20 standard
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD            20 )
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED   ON )
set(CMAKE_CXX_EXTENSIONS          OFF)
set(CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS ON )

# Find dependencies
find_package(ament_cmake REQUIRED)
find_package(rclcpp REQUIRED)
find_package(package_interfaces REQUIRED)

set(DEPENDENCIES
  rclcpp
  package_interfaces
)

# Include directories
include_directories(include)

# Single executable
add_executable(${PROJECT_NAME}_node
    src/main.cpp
    src/ros2/node.cpp
    src/logic/controller.cpp
    # ... other sources
)
ament_target_dependencies(${PROJECT_NAME}_node ${DEPENDENCIES})

# Install
install(
  TARGETS ${PROJECT_NAME}_core ${PROJECT_NAME}_ros2
  EXPORT export_${PROJECT_NAME}
  ARCHIVE DESTINATION lib
  LIBRARY DESTINATION lib
  RUNTIME DESTINATION bin
  INCLUDES DESTINATION include
)
install(
  TARGETS ${PROJECT_NAME}_node
  DESTINATION lib/${PROJECT_NAME}
)
install(DIRECTORY include/ DESTINATION include)
install(DIRECTORY launch/ config/ DESTINATION share/${PROJECT_NAME})

# Testing
if(BUILD_TESTING)
    find_package(launch_testing_ament_cmake REQUIRED)
    add_launch_test(test/test_e2e.py)
endif()

# Packaging
ament_package()
```

### package.xml

**Mandatory Fields:**

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<package format="3">
  <name>package_name</name>
  <version>1.0.0</version>
  <description>Clear package description</description>
  <maintainer email="dev@TODO.com"> Team</maintainer>
  <license>Proprietary</license>

  <buildtool_depend>ament_cmake</buildtool_depend>

  <depend>rclcpp</depend>
  <!-- ... other dependencies -->

  <test_depend>ament_cmake_gtest</test_depend>
  <test_depend>launch_testing_ament_cmake</test_depend>

  <export>
    <build_type>ament_cmake</build_type>
  </export>
</package>
```

## ✅ Quality Gates

### Structure Validation

**Pattern 1: Modular Architecture**

- [ ] Correct directory organization (core/ + ros2_interface/)
- [ ] Business logic separated from ROS2
- [ ] main.cpp contains only initialization
- [ ] Launch files in launch/ directory
- [ ] Configuration files in config/ directory
- [ ] Tests in test/ directory
- [ ] Documentation in docs/ directory

**Pattern 2: Simplified Architecture**

- [ ] Correct directory organization (logic/ + ros2/)
- [ ] Business logic separated from ROS2
- [ ] main.cpp contains only initialization
- [ ] Launch files in launch/ directory
- [ ] Configuration files in config/ directory
- [ ] Tests in test/ directory
- [ ] Documentation in docs/ directory

### Build Validation

**Pattern 1: Modular Architecture**

- [ ] Separate libraries for core and ROS2
- [ ] Core library has NO rclcpp dependency
- [ ] All targets compile without warnings
- [ ] Install rules for executables and resources

**Pattern 2: Simplified Architecture**

- [ ] Single executable approach
- [ ] Business logic separated from ROS2
- [ ] All targets compile without warnings
- [ ] Install rules for executables and resources

### Test Validation

**Pattern 1: Modular Architecture**

- [ ] Unit tests for business logic
- [ ] E2E tests with launch_testing
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] Test coverage > 80% for business logic

**Pattern 2: Simplified Architecture**

- [ ] E2E tests with launch_testing
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] Functional validation complete

### Documentation Validation

- [ ] README.md with overview
- [ ] Architecture documentation
- [ ] Interface documentation
- [ ] Testing documentation

---

_ROS 2 package structure standards ensuring clean, maintainable, and testable robot applications._
